# The coder stance for the coder-driven prompt variant: one procedure, the
# shell mechanics a worker needs to read its own results, and the verdict line
# that ends a turn.
#
# One register for every model, where the shipped stance branches on the
# resolved model id and carries two full procedures. Plain imperative
# sentences, one idea each, no metaphor — the register `docs/delegated-coder.md`
# argues for. Dropping the branch is a second variable in any A/B against a
# frontier model; see the README beside this file.
#
# The text lives in the companion Markdown rather than a shell string: a
# redirect keeps trailing newlines and skips stdout limits, and the prose is
# then diffable against the shipped stance without reading around quoting.
set -e
kj block create --role system --kind text --content-type text/markdown < "$(dirname "$0")/$(basename "$0" .kai).md"
